1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
[dramatic music playing]

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
[grunts]

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] Wait a second.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
I saw him on the stairs before.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Did he do it?

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
[Killua] Sorry, but I'm
a little pissed off right now,

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
so I'm just gonna
take it all out on you.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
-[tense music playing]
-[electricity crackling]

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
[opening theme music playing]

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

11
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
[singer singing in English]

12
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,000
[singer singing in English]

14
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

15
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
[singer singing in English]

16
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

17
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
STRONG X OR X WEAK

18
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
[electricity crackling, humming]

19
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] Huh? He's gone!

20
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[electricity crackling]

21
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
[screaming]

22
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
[groans]

23
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
[growls]

24
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
[tense music playing]

25
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,000
[Killua] Godspeed.

26
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
[narrator] With no time whatsoever
to roar or transform,

27
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Killua easily incapacitated Youpi.

28
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Such was the disparity in initiative.

29
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Killua's Godspeed
electrified his entire body,

30
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
allowing him to reach speeds
so high that they transcended

31
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,000
even the broadest limits
of his physical potential.

32
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,000
As it turned out,

33
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Killua had divided this power
into two core functions.

34
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
The first was called
Speed of Lightning

35
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
and gave him control
at superhuman speed.

36
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
The second let him respond
automatically to his opponent

37
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,000
and was called Whirlwind.

38
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,000
In a previous fight,
he'd used the latter

39
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
to stop his opponent's
fish dart in its tracks.

40
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
It was a preprogrammed response

41
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
to what was clearly malevolent intent
in his enemy's aura.

42
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
A reflex
that actually served to bypass

43
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
the comparatively slow human brain,

44
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
it proved more than sufficient

45
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
in surpassing
the enemy's physical speed.

46
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
[Menthuthuyoupi]
What in the hell is going on here?

47
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
These attacks,
in terms of sheer power,

48
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
they're all less than a tenth
of my own strength.

49
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
This doesn't make any sense.

50
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
I can't do a thing against him.

51
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
[Killua] Whirlwind.

52
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] Unreal.

53
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:42,000
This aura stuff is really intense.

54
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
[chuckles]

55
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
This is getting kinda interesting.

56
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Before my explosion,
I never would have enjoyed

57
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,000
fighting an uphill battle.

58
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
[narrator] This change in attitude

59
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
would lead Youpi to a surprising choice.

60
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
However, this would
not happen until later.

61
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
[Menthuthuyoupi chuckles]

62
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,000
[electricity crackling stops]

63
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
[gasps]

64
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
[Killua] Oops.

65
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Damn. I used it up already.

66
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Hold it!

67
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
You're never getting away
from me, you brat!

68
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,000
You and I are gonna
see this through to the end,

69
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,000
when you die!

70
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Huh?

71
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:31,000
He disappeared? Again?

72
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:35,000
That little jerk just vanished
like he never existed.

73
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
That's it.

74
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
At least one of them
must have the ability

75
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
to appear and disappear at will.

76
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
It's the only way at all
that any of this makes sense!

77
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,000
[dramatic music playing]

78
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,000
[Bloster] Huh?

79
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,000
[automated voice]
Please enter your code number.

80
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Aw, damn it.
I don't have a code number.

81
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Um…

82
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,000
[beeps]

83
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
[automated voice] Your code and data
do not match.

84
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Please reenter your code number.

85
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:19,000
A second input error will result
in your immediate restraint.

86
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
[Ikalgo] Don't tell me.
Did he really come down here

87
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
without knowing
about the code system?

88
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Okay, that didn't work.

89
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Guess I'll just have to get out.

90
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,000
[beeps]

91
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
[automated voice]
The door has been locked.

92
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Please enter your code number.

93
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
[Ikalgo] This is it.
I have two options.

94
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
The elevator will eventually fill
with sleeping gas.

95
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Once he's asleep,
I'll have to decide.

96
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:52,000
One, I just leave Bloster there
in the elevator,

97
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
and then I head for the surface
using the freight entrance.

98
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,000
MONITOR ROOM

99
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
That way, when he wakes up,

100
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,000
he'll still be stuck in the elevator.

101
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,000
But there's a high risk

102
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
that someone upstairs
will notice something's wrong.

103
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Two, I move Bloster
somewhere else

104
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
while he's knocked out.

105
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:15,000
There are plenty
of parked cars around,

106
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,000
and the warehouse doors

107
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
need a code to open them
from the inside.

108
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:23,000
He won't be able to open them
when he wakes up.

109
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Plus, I want to avoid
running into anyone if I can.

110
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
If I go upstairs
using the freight elevator,

111
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
there's much less
of a chance that'll happen.

112
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,000
No! That'll never work.

113
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
I have to kill Bloster
while he's asleep.

114
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,000
That's the safest way.

115
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Then I'll have to take control
of Bloster's corpse

116
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,000
and use it to take out
the other Squadron Leaders.

117
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
It's the least I could do.

118
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,000
I'll stick the barrel of my gun
through the gap in his armor,

119
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
and then I'll open fire!

120
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[narrator] Although Ikalgo's ability
allowed him to control corpses,

121
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
he had never actually
killed anyone before.

122
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
[automated voice]
Enter your code number immediately.

123
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,000
If an authorized code number

124
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,000
is not entered
within the next 30 seconds,

125
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
you will be taken into custody.

126
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
[grumbles]

127
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,000
[Ikalgo] The surveillance room
in the guard station.

128
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,000
There should be a feed

129
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
from the security camera
in the elevator

130
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
and a control to open the doors.

131
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
[keypad beeping]

132
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
-[gasps]
-[automatic gunfire]

133
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
[Bloster grunts]

134
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Well, I'm out, but it's too bad

135
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
I had to completely
destroy the elevator

136
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
so I could get free.

137
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Now, are there any other exits?

138
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
[tense music playing]

139
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
[Ikalgo] I was naive.

140
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,000
I didn't think
he'd shoot up the door.

141
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,000
What now? Do I wait for him
to lower his guard,

142
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
then sneak out
the freight entrance?

143
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Or should I be patient
and wait for him to leave?

144
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Either way,
if he goes back upstairs…

145
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
[grunting]

146
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
No! That's not good enough.

147
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
That's weak.

148
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
But if he goes back up to the surface

149
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
and tells the others that Flutter's dead,

150
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
I'll be able to move around
without fear.

151
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Idiot!

152
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
If I let an enemy return to the surface,

153
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,000
the danger increases for everyone.

154
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,000
I can't.

155
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Huh?

156
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
[groans]

157
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
[grunts]

158
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,000
[grumbles]

159
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Man, that one is pretty thick.

160
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,000
[tense music playing]

161
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Huh?

162
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
[grumbles]

163
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
[Ikalgo] I can't let him
go back upstairs.

164
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:45,000
If I can't stop him,
I have no right to be here.

165
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
[Bloster grumbles]

166
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
[Ikalgo] Come on. Come on.

167
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
Right into my trap.

168
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Almost there.

169
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Wait till he's a little farther from it.

170
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
[dramatic music playing]

171
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
[gasps]

172
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
[Ikalgo] Now!

173
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Agh!

174
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:00,000
[Bloster] So there really
was someone besides Flutter.

175
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
If I didn't know better,

176
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
I'd think you were trying
to lure me in there.

177
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
-[Ikalgo groans]
-[Bloster chuckles]

178
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Too bad for you.

179
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
If only one path remains,

180
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:14,000
it's just too good to be true.
Anyone would be suspicious.

181
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Well, now I know you exist,
so that's something.

182
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,000
[laughs]

183
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
And I bet you're hiding
in the surveillance room

184
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:25,000
to observe me, you chicken!

185
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
[Ikalgo] Damn it. I was so close

186
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
to having him completely
trapped in that corridor,

187
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,000
but there's no way out
from where he is now.

188
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
He's still trapped.

189
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Sleeping gas
will fill the room eventually,

190
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
and when it does…

191
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
[gasps] No! He isn't trapped!

192
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
There's still a way out!

193
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
[Bloster] I should probably
get out of here.

194
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:54,000
I'm willing to bet
that's sleeping gas.

195
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:59,000
[Ikalgo] I have to do something
before he figures it out.

196
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Wait. The armored vehicles
in the garage.

197
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,000
With those,
I could at least lock him in,

198
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
but then I'll have no way
to get back upstairs.

199
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Think. Is there anything here I can use?

200
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:18,000
I've gotta think of a plan, fast!

201
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,000
[Bloster] Looks like I'm gonna have
to blow through this bulkhead.

202
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Man, this is really getting
to be a pain in the rear.

203
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
[Ikalgo] I've gotta do it!

204
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
[gunfire]

205
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:45,000
[Bloster] Damn. All that,
and I barely scorched the surface?

206
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
I guess I'm just gonna have
to come up

207
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
with something else then.

208
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
I know!

209
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
The bulkhead controls
are in the monitor room,

210
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,000
so I can go over there
to open the bulkheads.

211
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Now we're talkin'.

212
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Wait. I have to go
through a bulkhead

213
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:05,000
to reach the monitor room.

214
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Damn it all.

215
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Looks like I'm still
gonna have to destroy this one

216
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
if I want any chance
of getting back upstairs.

217
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Hang on.

218
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
I wonder.
There might be a way to escape

219
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
without busting down a bulkhead.

220
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,000
Huh?

221
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
It's opening?

222
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Is that a tank? [scoffs]

223
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,000
That's exactly the kind of thing
a gutless chicken would use.

224
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
But the bulkhead behind it's still shut,

225
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
and the door to the monitor room
is just beyond it.

226
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Okay, that can only mean one thing.

227
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
First, he closed the front bulkhead,

228
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,000
and then he parked the vehicle there.

229
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Then he returned to the monitor room

230
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:02,000
and started raising the front bulkhead
and lowering the back one.

231
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Once he did,
he raced back to the vehicle.

232
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Doesn't that mean
that he's trapped, too?

233
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
He blocked off his only escape route

234
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
just to force a showdown?

235
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Hah! You're kidding.

236
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Seriously? Come on.

237
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
[laughs]

238
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
So I guess there must be
someone else around here,

239
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:29,000
and they must be sitting up
in the control room watching me.

240
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,000
How dare they?

241
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Well, watch this, you peeping Tom,

242
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,000
because I'm about to drag
your little buddy

243
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:41,000
out of this tank
and rip him to shreds!

244
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
[Ikalgo] I'm the only one here,

245
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:49,000
and I'm gonna have
to take care of this.

246
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Man, that armor's tough.

247
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
[Bloster gasps]

248
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
[grunts]

249
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,000
[gulps]

250
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,000
[grunts]

251
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,000
[Ikalgo] I did it.

252
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Ah, damn it.

253
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
The bastard blocked the elevator.

254
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,000
If he hadn't done that,

255
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
I could have blown a hole
in the ceiling

256
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
and climbed up the cable.

257
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:30,000
[tense music playing]

258
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,000
[Ikalgo] I've blocked his escape route.

259
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,000
First hurdle cleared.

260
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Hmm? Man, you've got a lot of nerve,
you know that, buddy?

261
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,000
I'm gonna pump you full of bullets.

262
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Hmm?

263
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Smoke, huh?

264
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,000
So, is he dead?

265
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Did he already lose?

266
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Either way, there's no way
to move this thing.

267
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
The gap's only a few centimeters.

268
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
The entrance is completely blocked.

269
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,000
[roars]

270
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
[groans]

271
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Now, come out!

272
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Your friend is gonna burn to death!

273
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:32,000
If you act now,
I'm willing to spare you!

274
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Open the damned bulkhead!
You hear me?

275
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,000
[Ikalgo] Being an octopus,

276
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,000
I only need a few centimeters
to squeeze through.

277
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Second hurdle cleared.

278
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,000
[Bloster] Hey!

279
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Open the bulkhead!

280
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,000
[coughing]

281
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:56,000
[Ikalgo] Now I just have to wait
for the sleeping gas to fill the room.

282
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
[Bloster coughing]

283
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
[groaning, coughing]

284
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
[Ikalgo] I can hold my breath,

285
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
but I don't want to waste
any more time.

286
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
I've gotta wait for the right moment.

287
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,000
[Bloster coughing]

288
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,000
[thud]

289
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,000
[grunts]

290
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:29,000
[dramatic music playing]

291
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
[Ikalgo] Third hurdle cleared.

292
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Don't rush.

293
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Nice and slow.

294
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,000
This is the final hurdle.

295
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
[gags]

296
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Just pull the trigger, and I'm done.

297
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,000
[heart beating]

298
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
[grunting]

299
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
This is the best option.

300
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
If I can take control of his corpse,

301
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
it'll be a lot safer upstairs,

302
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
so I've gotta do this!

303
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
There's… There's nobody else here.

304
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:31,000
There's no one else to help me!

305
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
I have to do this!

306
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
I have to!

307
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
[gagging]

308
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
[gagging]

309
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
[sobbing]

310
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:11,000
There's no way. I can't do it…

311
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:17,000
because I'm a coward!

312
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,000
[sobbing]

313
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,000
[narrator] Meanwhile, as Ikalgo
was lamenting his weakness,

314
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Morel was within
the shifted central tower

315
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
facing off against Pouf's pupa,

316
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:36,000
but in addition to the physical fight
that would soon begin,

317
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Morel was battling
serious doubts of his own.

318
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
[Morel] Hold on. What if…

319
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:49,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] Pitou, Pouf,
are you there? Answer me!

320
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:53,000
[Morel] What if no one
responded to Youpi's call

321
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,000
not because they chose to,

322
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,000
but because they weren't able to?

323
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:03,000
The pupa should just be
a goopy mess right now,

324
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
not a fully-formed creature.

325
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:10,000
If he's utterly defenseless
while he changes forms,

326
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
this is the best chance
I'm gonna get.

327
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
Time to attack!

328
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:19,000
He made a mistake,
a fatal one.

329
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,000
How could he have done that
in this situation?

330
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,000
It's not possible.
This has to be a trap.

331
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,000
There's no doubt in my mind.

332
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,000
The only question now

333
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,000
is whether it's a trap
that's already been activated

334
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:39,000
without me doing
anything to trigger it,

335
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
or whether it'll be activated
as soon as I attack.

336
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,000
Which is it?

337
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[Shaiapouf]
You are having these doubts,

338
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,000
because you are exceptional.

339
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:57,000
However, that's all there is to it.

340
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,000
[closing theme music playing]

341
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:06,000
[Morel] So should I attack or not?

342
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,000
What do I do?

343
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:15,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

344
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[upbeat music playing]

345
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
[Gon] Next time, "Fake and Real."

346
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,000
Hey, if not now, then when?

347
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,000
[Killua] No! Not yet, fool!

348
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:43,000
[Gon] You're not Killua. You're a fake.

349
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:48,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
